<title>BRAZIL: Brazil oil/gas reserves at 14.1 barrels in 1996.</title>
<headline>Brazil oil/gas reserves at 14.1 barrels in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian oil and gas reserves reached 14.1 billion barrels at the end of 1996, state oil firm Petrobras said in a statement.</p>
<p>Of this total, 11.6 billion barrels were oil reserves and 2.5 billion barrels were gas reserves, the company said.</p>
<p>The statement said oil and gas reserves were up 28 percent over the previous year as 2.7 billion barrels were added to the country's reserves.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
</text>
